Lab 2: Synchronizing Repositories
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the fundamentals of repository synchronization in Red Hat Satellite
Configure and synchronize content from Red Hat repositories to Satellite
Add and configure custom third-party repositories
Verify successful content synchronization through the Satellite web interface
Troubleshoot common synchronization issues
Implement best practices for repository management
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) package management
Knowledge of YUM/DNF repository concepts
Understanding of Red Hat Satellite architecture from Lab 1
Access to Red Hat Customer Portal credentials (for demonstration purposes)
Basic networking concepts (HTTP/HTTPS, proxy configurations)
Lab Environment Setup
Ready-to-Use Cloud Machines: Al Nafi provides pre-configured Linux-based cloud machines for this lab. Simply click Start Lab to access your environment - no need to build your own virtual machines or install software.

