Task 1: Synchronize Content from Red Hat to Satellite
Subtask 1.1: Access Satellite Web Interface
Open your web browser and navigate to your Satellite server:

https://satellite.example.com
Log in using the administrator credentials:

Username: admin
Password: redhat123 (or as provided in your lab environment)
Verify the dashboard loads successfully and shows the main Satellite interface.

Subtask 1.2: Configure Red Hat Repository Synchronization
Navigate to Content Management:

Click on Content in the main menu
Select Red Hat Repositories
Enable Red Hat Enterprise Linux repositories:

Expand Red Hat Enterprise Linux for x86_64
Locate Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8 for x86_64 - BaseOS (RPMs)
Click the toggle switch to Enable this repository
Repeat for Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8 for x86_64 - AppStream (RPMs)
Configure repository settings:

Click on the repository name to access detailed settings
Verify the Download Policy is set to Immediate
Note the Repository URL and GPG Key information
Subtask 1.3: Initiate Repository Synchronization
Start synchronization process:

Navigate to Content > Products
Find Red Hat Enterprise Linux for x86_64
Click on the product name
Select Repositories tab
Click Select Action > Sync Now for each enabled repository
Monitor synchronization progress:

Navigate to Monitor > Tasks
Look for tasks with names like "Synchronize repository"
Click on individual tasks to view detailed progress
Verify initial sync completion:

# SSH to Satellite server and check sync status
hammer repository list --organization "Default Organization"
